  "goodToKnow": "Der Dackel (also Dachshund or Teckel) is a dachshund, bred in Germany to hunt badgers (Dachse) in their burrows. It's often seen as a symbol of German Gemütlichkeit and stubbornness. The first official Olympic mascot, Waldi, a colourful dachshund, represented the 1972 Munich Games. Der Dackelblick is a pleading puppy-dog look. The plural is the same: die Dackel."
